❮ Java Keywords

Theinstanceofkeyword checks whether an object is an instance of a specific class or 
an interface.

The instanceof keyword compares the instance with type. The return value is eithertrueorfalse.

Read more about objects in ourJava Classes/Objects Tutorial.

❮ Java Keywords

### Code Examples

```
Example
Check whether an object is an instance of a specific class:
public class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Main myObj = new Main();
    System.out.println(myObj instanceof Main); // returns true
  }
}
Try it Yourself »
```

